    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive outlook for the Austin Waves is anchored by high-ceiling matchups against middle-of-the-road pitching, with **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) leading the charge. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a favorable 4.63 xERA matchup against Littell, and while the opposing battery limits his base-stealing ceiling by 2%, his high floor makes him our most reliable play for volume. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is maximized by a 4.41 xERA opponent and a strong dynamic platoon advantage, which elevates his projection well above his base level. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** remain elite options despite tougher individual assignments; **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s score of 70.51 is bolstered significantly by favorable park factors and order placement, while **Kyle Tucker** provides consistent, high-value production despite facing a slightly more stingy arm in Painter.\n\nOur roster flexibility remains constrained by the IL, leaving **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Drake Baldwin** unavailable, which simplifies the bench depth. The most marginal call today was between **Josh Jung** (58.60) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.23). While both fall into the \"marginal\" tier, **Josh Jung** ultimately secured the start due to a neutral platoon edge and a stronger base projection against Wacha, whereas **Miguel Vargas** faced slight downward pressure on his score due to park factor disadvantages. **Brayan Rocchio** sits at the bottom of our active lineup (40.91); his status is precarious, but he retains his spot primarily due to the lack of available alternatives. We are closely monitoring the weather and lineup confirmations for **Liam Hicks**, who faces a high-skill opponent in McLean (3.03 xERA); if his order position slips or wind conditions shift, we may see his efficiency drop further, but for now, he stays in the active slot to maintain our daily game caps.",
